@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/blocks@>
@
The file and print options, in their short, long, and = forms; an option value must be a separate word or follow =.
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/Cases@/blocks@=
test_case blocks tests/cases/blocks
prints msg Hello --file=archive.la -p msg
prints line Hi -f archive.la -p line
prints nest '!' -f archive.la -p base
prints separate Hello -f=archive.la -p=msg
fails attached "flag provided but not defined: -farchive.la" -farchive.la -pmsg
@| litar command@:UI@/Command Line@/Test@/run case@+binaries@+test fixtures @
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/compose@>
@
A node evaluates the blocks of its base before its own, and an archive outside every composition is refused.
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/Cases@/compose@=
test_case compose tests/cases/compose
prints root base -f base.la -p msg
prints child basechild -f child.la -p msg
fails unknown "could not find archive 'nope.la'" -f nope.la -p msg
@| litar command@:UI@/Command Line@/Test@/run case@+binaries@+test fixtures @
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/errors@>
@
Every misuse of the command line fails with its message on stderr and nothing on stdout.
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/Cases@/errors@=
test_case errors tests/cases/errors
fails none "missing -p, --print, -l, --literal, -e, --effective, -d, --depend, -r, --reference, or -a, --agent"
fails combine "cannot combine print and literal" -p a -l a
fails combine-rev "cannot combine print and literal" -l a -p b
fails nofile "missing -f, --file" -p msg
fails unknown "flag provided but not defined: -t" -t . -p msg
fails cluster "flag provided but not defined: -al" -al
fails positional "Usage: litar " archive.la
fails missing "chunk 'missing' is not defined" -f archive.la -p missing
fails long "chunk 'missing' is not defined" --file archive.la --print missing
fails long-eq "chunk 'missing' is not defined" --file=archive.la -print=missing
prints depend-empty '' -f archive.la -d nope
fails effective "chunk 'missing' is not defined" -f archive.la -e missing
@| litar command@:UI@/Command Line@/Test@/run case@+binaries@+test fixtures @
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/filter@>
@
A filter transforms its input; one without a shebang or with a failing exit status fails the evaluation.
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/Cases@/filter@=
test_case filter tests/cases/filter
prints upper HELLO -f archive.la -p msg
fails noshebang "filter 'bad' has no shebang" -f archive.la -p use
fails status "filter 'die' exited with status 3" -f archive.la -p use2
@| litar command@:UI@/Command Line@/Test@/run case@+binaries@+test fixtures @
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/fuse@>
@
A filter sees the files of its view, read-only below an overlay; the case needs /dev/fuse.
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/Cases@/fuse@=
test_case fuse tests/cases/fuse
[ -e /dev/fuse ] || skip "no /dev/fuse"
prints cat 'hello world' -f archive.la -p msg
prints exe $'yes\n' -f archive.la -p ask
prints overlay overlay -f archive.la -p made
fails readonly "exited with status" -f archive.la -p row
fails missing "file 'missing' is not defined" -f archive.la -p '@@|show@@,missing'
fails badpath "invalid file path '../x'" -f archive.la -p '@@|show@@,../x'
@| litar command@:UI@/Command Line@/Test@/run case@+binaries@+test fixtures @
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/help@>
@
The usage is printed for -h and --help wherever they stand, unless they are the value of another option.
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/Cases@/help@=
test_case help
usage=$(cat <<'END'
Usage: litar [-a] [-f ARCHIVE] [-l CHUNK_REFERENCE] [-e CHUNK_REFERENCE] [-d CHUNK_REFERENCE] [-r ITEM] [-p EXPRESSION]

-h, --help: print the usage
-a, --agent: open an MCP server to handle the requests from agents
-f, --file ARCHIVE: specify the archive file, find the composition and the node corresponding
-l, --literal CHUNK_REFERENCE: print the blocks applied to CHUNK_REFERENCE literally
-e, --effective CHUNK_REFERENCE: print the effective blocks of CHUNK_REFERENCE
-d, --depend CHUNK_REFERENCE: list all blocks that depend on CHUNK_REFERENCE
-r, --reference ITEM: list all blocks that refer to ITEM
-p, --print EXPRESSION: evaluate EXPRESSION, and print it
END
)
prints help "$usage"$'\n' --help
prints short-h "$usage"$'\n' -h
prints help-after-other "$usage"$'\n' -p x --help
fails help-as-value "missing -f, --file" -p --help
@| litar command@:UI@/Command Line@/Test@/run case@+binaries@+test fixtures @
@<Project@/litar@/Tests@/case results@+
@<.@/Cases@/list@>
@
